        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0573" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg477"/>

                <head>No. 367.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hale
                        to Mr. Thomas.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-09-26"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 26,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 2, under date of July 26,
                    relating to recent political disturbances in Peru, has been received.</p>
                <p>The indignation of the people of Peru at a cruel assassination and an attempted
                    usurpation and overthrow of a representative government commands admiration, and
                    their calm return to order gives promise of a stable condition of public
                    affairs.</p>
                <p>Your reply to the circular-note of Doctor Caso’s is approved.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES HALE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
